etymology_text:
From Russian журна́л (žurnál),
from French journal,
from Latin diurnālis, from diēs (“day”).

From Proto-Turkic *umnït- (“to forget”).
Cognate with Cognate with Old Turkic [script needed] (unıt-, “to forget”);
Kazakh ұмыту (umıtuw, “to forget”), Kyrgyz унутуу (unutuu, “to forget”), Southern Altai ундыыр (undïïr, “to forget”), Khakas ундирға (undirğa, “to forget”), Uzbek unutmoq (“to forget”), Turkmen unutmak (“to forget”), Turkish unutmak (“to forget”).

From Proto-Turkic *üŕeŋgü (“stirrup”), from *yüŕeŋgü, from *yüŕ (“ring”).
Cognate with
Old Turkic [script needed] (üzeŋü, “stirrup”);
Kazakh үзеңгі (üzeŋgi), Southern Altai ӱзеҥи (üzeŋi), Uyghur ئۈزەڭگە (üzengge), Uzbek uzangi, Turkmen üzeňňi, Azerbaijani üzəngi, Turkish üzengi (“stirrup”);
Yakut иҥэһэ (iŋehe) (with metathesis), Chuvash йӑрана (jărana, “stirrup”), etc.
